                <pb facs="0418" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg344"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">I. N. Proeschel to the Rev. Messrs. Jaulmes and
                        Pulsford.</hi></head>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 20, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen:</hi> The minister of the United States has
                    charged me to acknowledge to you the reception of the address which you have
                    been pleased to transmit to him in the name of the French Methodist conference,
                    and to assure you of the pleasure with which he will en, deavor to cause it to
                    reach the widow of our lamented President.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the assurance of my most respectful consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>I. N. PROESCHEL, <hi rendition="#italic">Private
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. Pastors <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Jaulmes</hi> and <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">L. Pulsford.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
